{"title":"2023 SSMO Relay Round 4 Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_SSMO_Relay_Round_4_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Martha starts out with the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> on her calculator, which has three buttons that multiply the current number by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/7547747b133453d3c209cff6cfbf129aa67a6947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/3/5533bc48602603f16d18c04858cad119c04833c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> respectively. She randomly presses one of the buttons four times. After these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> presses, she cubes the number. The expected value of the final number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/8/888fed89e19182447f85b3cb6676548a49395284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"27\" height=\"34\" /> for relatively prime positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd923e41635af40a1abe58f230732f2280b0723a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db26f75f6218a382840f0ed34f5d36bcff61d33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_SSMO_Relay_Round_1_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2023 SSMO Relay Round 1 Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_SSMO_Relay_Round_4_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/5/9f5a161f3c51a7f0fa26d26396ca7f05cd398a2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T=$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> TNYWR. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/7/ab7a9fc96ffbe4a931681d9487e23dd4ab7fd7a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\left\\lfloor\\sqrt{N}\\right\\rfloor.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"96\" height=\"34\" /> Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> points are chosen on the sides of a triangle with area 1 such that there is at least one point on each side. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> be the area of the polygon formed by connecting the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> points in counterclockwise order. Find the expected value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/b/98b39d52d3ce0dcf6b667c281c6bda351e9267ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{30}{1-m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"53\" height=\"40\" />\n(Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/3/8335b7060b06a6a8a75d96c843490ef7caaf1602.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\{x\\right\\} = x - \\lfloor x \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"114\" height=\"20\" />)\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_SSMO_Relay_Round_1_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2023 SSMO Relay Round 1 Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_SSMO_Relay_Round_4_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/5/9f5a161f3c51a7f0fa26d26396ca7f05cd398a2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T=$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> TNYWR. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/f/a7fc8f668ffc0730528bca6447b71e28cebd0cf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" /> numbers are chosen from the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/2/9a26e6d173bffb93bb7a159db4d8130b7ce6e352.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,2,3,\\dots,N+1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"152\" height=\"20\" /> with replacement. If the probability that the median of these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/f/a7fc8f668ffc0730528bca6447b71e28cebd0cf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" /> numbers is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/a/0daebf82804290f3e62edddcf479332f7d1d3fd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{N+2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"54\" height=\"39\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/a/52a0c0a33e764fdc62793675f3974a6f8f9c5ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"22\" height=\"16\" /> such that the decimal representation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/d/35d28b320613cdb8c221307e9365cdd65fcb9449.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{M}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"25\" height=\"38\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />'s before the first nonzero digit of it, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> rounded to nearest multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b835f2c6c592edc4583ce996f86bcc0d07ca8da5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_SSMO_Relay_Round_1_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2023 SSMO Relay Round 1 Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018065246\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.014 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.022 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 123/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4809/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:26387:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018065246 and revision id 247862. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}